This README file contains the steps necesssary to configure
machines to run the Orbix services and run OpenI-DEAS.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Instructions for Setup:
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

1) If OrbixE2A is being installed on a machine that also has
   Orbix3 installed on it, then rename /etc/orbix_profile to
   /etc/orbix3_profile. Otherwise, you can skip this step.

   mv /etc/orbix_profile /etc/orbix3_profile

2) Edit the the /etc/profile to point to the new orbix profiles.
   If Orbix3 is installed on the machine then there should
   already be a section of code similar to the following:

   if [ -r /etc/orbix_profile ]
   then
   .  /etc/orbix_profile
   fi

   If this is the case, then leave these lines in and enter in
   the following lines directly above:

   if [ -r /etc/orbix3_profile ]
   then
   .  /etc/orbix3_profile
   fi

   This way, both orbix profiles should be run. If Orbix3 is not
   installed on the machine, then simply add the following lines
   somewhere in /etc/profile (usually near the end):

   if [ -r /etc/orbix_profile ]
   then
   .  /etc/orbix_profile
   fi

3) Copy the new Orbix E2A orbix_profile into the /etc directory

   cp <path_to_script>/orbix_profile /etc/orbix_profile


4) Source the new /etc/orbix_profile

  . /etc/orbix_profile


5) Run only one of the scripts mentioned below.

   a) To configure the one machine that will be running the Orbix
      configuration, location, and naming services:

      <path_to_script>/deployServicesDomain.pl [<network alias>]

      where <network alias> is an optional parameter that represents
      an alias of the machine that is being configured. This makes
      it easier to move the machine where the configuration resides.
      This parameter will probably be "cvgoi10".

   b) To configure the machines that will be connecting to the Orbix
      configuration, location, and naming services running on
      the machine above:

      <path_to_script>/deployLinkedDomain.pl <hostname of config machine>

      where <hostname of config machine> will probably be "cvgoi10".


6) Verify daemon(s) are running:

   ps -ef | grep it

7) Update the boot scripts:

   On SGI:
   cp itsvs_openideas10 /etc/init.d/
   chmod 755 /etc/init.d/itsvs_openideas10
   cd /etc/rc2.d
   ln -s ../init.d/itsvs_openideas10 S99openideas10

   On HP:
   cp itsvs_openideas10 /etc/init.d/
   chmod 755 /etc/init.d/itsvs_openideas10
   cd /etc/rc2.d
   ln -s ../init.d/itsvs_openideas10 S900openideas10

   On IBM:
   cp itsvs_openideas10 /etc/
   chmod 755 /etc/itsvs_openideas10
   Add the call to run /etc/itsvs_openideas10 to the end of /etc/rc.local

   On Sun:
   cp itsvs_openideas10 /etc/init.d/
   chmod 755 /etc/init.d/itsvs_openideas10
   cd /etc/rc2.d
   ln -s ../init.d/itsvs_openideas10 S99openideas10
